    "result_text": "The full build passes with all tests green (the surefire config runs `AcceptanceTest`, which covers both the new SILVER and BRONZE cases).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` field for owners:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (documenting the SILVER/BRONZE rule), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` plus a small `formatMembershipTier(owner)` default method that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`. This sits alongside the existing derived-field helpers (`formatDisplayName`, `formatInitials`, `formatMembershipNumber`), keeping DTO-derivation logic in one consistent place with a single responsibility, and it safely handles null `namesakeCount`/blank email.\n\nBoth `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` pass; **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
